        openings: ("Five patients at a clinic found credit cards opened in their names, and the lookups trace to {D}'s login. The applications were mailed to {D}'s address. This is not {DL}'s first time here, since {PRIORDATE} brought {D.him} in once already after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "The front desk computer is shared, and a coworker used {D.his} login as well. A login is not a person, and the mailing address could have been picked by someone else."),
