        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Fire Truck Moved From Bay by Visitor", "Defendant From Ambulance Case Seen at Another Station"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Took property of {V}, a fire department, valued at $400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took gear from a fire truck and drove a department pickup around a lot. {DL} says {D.he} was only looking around.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Station Camera", "{D} climbs into the pickup."), E(.physical, 2, "Gear Bag", "Found in {D}'s car.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Looking", "{DL} says {D.he} was only looking.")],
        role: "Fire captain",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your role at the station.", "\"I'm the fire captain. I'm in charge of the crew, the trucks and the equipment, and I'm responsible for what leaves the station.\""), .direct("What did you find that morning?", "\"The department pickup was parked crooked, and a gear bag was missing from the fire truck. There was a note on the windshield.\""), .direct("What was in the gear bag?", "\"A set of turnout gear, a helmet and a few tools, together worth about $400.\""), .direct("What does the station camera show?", "\"It shows {D} walking in at midnight, climbing into the pickup, driving it around the lot, and then going to the truck.\""), .direct("Where was the bag found?", "\"In {DL}'s car, which deputies located later that day.\""), .direct("What did the note say?", "\"It had a name and a phone number, and the words 'I'll bring it back.' I gave it to the deputies.\""), .cross("Did {DL} damage the pickup?", "\"No. It was just moved around the lot.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to leave with the pickup?", "\"No. It stayed in the lot.\""), .cross("Did anyone call the number on the note?", "\"The deputies did. {D.He} answered and met them.\""), .cross("Did {DL} return the bag?", "\"Deputies recovered it from the car.\""), .cross("Was the station locked?", "\"The lot gate was open. The truck bays were closed.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took fire gear from a fire truck and drove a department pickup around a lot at midnight.", "{DL} was only looking around and left a note with a phone number."),
        allocution: "\"I took that gear and drove the department pickup around the lot because I was curious about the equipment. I meant to return it, and I left the truck where I found it. I'm sorry to the fire department. I've always admired the volunteers, and I should have asked.\"",
        truths: ("The camera shows {DL} climbing into the pickup, and a gear bag from the truck was in {D.his} car.", "{DL} left a note with a phone number saying {D.he} would return everything."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the gear bag?", "\"I took it from the truck, but I meant to bring it back. I left a note with my number.\""), .direct("Why were you at the station?", "\"I've always been curious about fire trucks. I walked in and looked around.\""), .direct("Why did you drive the pickup?", "\"The keys were in it. I drove it slowly around the lot and parked it. It was foolish.\""), .direct("Why did you take the bag?", "\"I wanted to see the gear. I put it in my car and meant to bring it back in the morning.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies called?", "\"I answered and met them. I handed over the bag and apologized.\""), .direct("What do you want to say to the fire department?", "\"I'm sorry for the trouble and for entering the lot. I'll do whatever they ask.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, I've been in this court before, and I should have known better than to walk into a fire department lot at midnight.\""), .cross("You entered a fire department lot at midnight, didn't you?", "\"I did walk into that lot at midnight, and I know that was wrong. I don't have a good reason except curiosity.\""), .cross("You took the bag without asking, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I took the gear bag without asking anyone, and I know that was wrong, even though I meant to bring it back with the note.\""), .cross("You drove a department pickup without permission, didn't you?", "\"Yes, around the lot, and I had no right to touch it. I took the keys off the hook while the others were at lunch.\""), .cross("Your note doesn't say what you took, does it?", "\"No, it only said I'd bring it back and gave my number. I should have written exactly what I had taken as well.\"")],
        openings: ("At midnight, the station camera shows {D} climbing into a department pickup and driving it around the lot. A gear bag worth about $400 from a fire truck was later found in {D}'s car, and {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}.", "{DL} was only looking around, and left a note with a phone number. A person who leaves a note giving their name and number did not mean to keep what was taken."),
